      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Transparent Pricing Breakdown for Car Transport From Guwahati To Bangalore</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><h3>Freight Cost Breakdown</h3>
<p>Understanding every line item in your shipping invoice is essential for accurate budgeting and forecasting. Below is a clear, concise breakdown of the five key components that shape your final freight quote.</p>
<p><strong>1. Base Freight</strong> – This is the foundational charge that reflects the distance, weight, and volume of your shipment. It sets the stage for all other adjustments.</p>
<p><strong>2. Fuel Surcharge</strong> – Fluctuations in oil prices are passed on through this variable fee. It ensures that carriers can maintain service levels despite rising fuel costs.</p>
<p><strong>3. Insurance Premium</strong> – Protects against loss or damage during transit. The premium is calculated as a percentage of the declared value and can be tailored to your risk tolerance.</p>
<p><strong>4. Loading Equipment Fee</strong> – Covers specialized equipment such as forklifts, pallet jacks, or container loading gear. This fee is incurred when your cargo requires handling beyond standard pallets.</p>
<p><strong>5. GST (Goods and Services Tax)</strong> – A statutory tax applied to the subtotal of all preceding charges, calculated at the prevailing rate in the destination country.</p>
<p>Below is a quick reference table that summarizes each component and its impact on the final quote.</p>
